      "id": 11469,
      "name": "phantaskippy",
      "username": "phantaskippy",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-10-31T19:59:43.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>This is updated from the one I posted in January, with a few minor tweaks to old ratings for better consistency and Vengeance heroes added in. &nbsp;I will update this again with my Cosmos ratings once that expansion is released.</p><p>Again, this is not a \"Which hero is best\" exercise, but an attempt to show where the strengths and weaknesses of each hero lie.</p><p>4 overarching categories, Offense, Defense, Support, Mechanics.</p><p>Each of those was then broken into 4 sub-categories, and those 4 categories where each given a 0-5 score, adding those up gave the overall for that category.</p><p><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheet/ccc?key=0Anq2XuBH6M1XdHZTenAwMzhWRF9xcmNQamViSGVIbmc&amp;usp=sharing\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">And here it is!</a></p><p>Note there is a second tab adjusted for Promo Character Cards.</p><p>Here's an explanation of each rating category so you can see how I judged them.</p><p>Offense:</p><p>Relieable damage: Given 2 cards in play, how many different combos deal damage, and how effectively (early game and small set up)</p><p>Damage Boosting: &nbsp;increasing damage dealt, yours and others (bonus for boosting more heroes)</p><p>One Shots: &nbsp;Damage dealt by one-shots</p><p>High End Damage: &nbsp;With all the cards you could want, how much can you throw down over several turns.</p><p>Defense:</p><p>Damage Reduction involves reducing damage taken by heroes</p><p>Damage Prevention involves reducing damage dealt by villains, being immune to damage and redirection away from heroes.</p><p>Healing is recovery for you and others</p><p>Tanking is redirecting damage away from a hero to a different hero. (usually yourself, but smoke bombs is also tanking)</p><p>Support:</p><p>Destruction: &nbsp;How much destruction the hero has, Environment and Ongoing, how many cards do it, how reliable is it, how much cost for doing so.</p><p>Ally Card Help: &nbsp;Putting cards in other hero's hands or in play.</p><p>Synergy: &nbsp;How well this deck makes other decks better in ways not already covered.</p><p>Deck Manipulation: &nbsp;Messing with non-hero decks ability to play cards, or what cards are in those decks.</p><p>Mechanics:</p><p>Search: &nbsp;Cards that pull cards from your deck or trash, and less reliable extra draws.</p><p>Base Power: &nbsp;If you have no cards in play how good is your power? &nbsp;(sucks to be AZ, Adept or Unity)</p><p>Card Draw/Play: &nbsp;How fast you can draw and/or play cards in general throughout the game.</p><p>Internal Combos: &nbsp;How well the deck interacts with itself in ways not covered already. (things like Legacy Ring, chaining Instruments etc.)</p>",
